    "description": "Apex Hyperclass 11T prototype: top-tier racing class, separate from Medium Rev4. Hover and roof nodes use predictive 45-degree physical gimbals, differential force alignment and an emergency x7 envelope (4.48 MN per four-node array). Surface retention is produced by roof thrusters, not direct forces; automatic airborne flight-frame torque is disabled. Hover-priority power allocation can progressively kill the rear engine. Apply AFTER 'Apply Physical Definition To Craft' so collider layout and node positions match.",
    "exportedUtc": "2026-07-24 (authored)",
    "units": "SI unless stated: kg, m, s, N, m/s, m/s2. Throttle/gain fields dimensionless.",
    "notes": "PHYSICAL VECTORING UPDATE. Continuous hover output and Kp/Kd remain unchanged. The x7 ceiling is reachable only by protected emergency/stabilizer channels. Test-drive loads reached 4.26-4.59 MN while the prior x5 envelope plateaued at 3.2 MN. Rear propulsion shedding begins when protected demand reaches 35% of reactor output and reaches full cut at 70%, recovering more slowly after the load passes. Gray/yellow/cyan/red Gizmo lines show mount/target/actual/applied thruster directions."
  },
